<p>Absolutely beautiful. I want to point out flaws but I can't find any. Be back once I reread to find something to nitpick. Upvoted!</p>
<p>Edit: Found it. I think &quot;destroyed&quot; is too general a term when referring to the Swedish capital. It would be extra horrifying/clinical (in keeping with the Foundation being cold) to specify the means of destruction. The city being firebombed out of existence, for example, hits a lot harder than merely &quot;destroying&quot; it. Firebombing is just an example, I'm sure there are better options.</p>
<p>In fact, I know this would be a lot of work and may not fit in to the whole plotline, but reading the transcript of the actual conversation about the city would be cool. Something about this help desk lady cheerfully advising someone to destroy an entire city is creepy in an awesome way.</p>

